<title>UK: ICI down in sympathy with BOC.</title>
<headline>ICI down in sympathy with BOC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Chemical Industries Plc dropped on Thursday, dragged lower by BOC Group Plc which fell after first-quarter results no better than analysts had expected, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;They are just down in sympathy with BOC,&quot; said one market-maker. BOC was down 10p at 928 by 0905 GMT while ICI was down 13-1/2p at 748-1/2.</p>
<p>Sources also said ICI and other stocks exposed to swings in the economic cycle in Germany and elsewhere in continental Europe had been hit by comments from the Bundesbank ruling out futher cuts in interest rates.</p>
<p>GKN was down 3p at 910-1/2, RMC Group Plc was down 2-1/2p at 935 and Redland Plc was down 3p at 347.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
